&lt;p&gt;Marketers need to know how to track brand visibility in AI search because search has changed. AI-generated answers now show up earlier in the discovery journey, often before a traditional search result. In 2025, nearly a third of Gen Z consumers (31%) defaulted to chatbots or AI to find information online, according to &lt;a href="https://offers.hubspot.com/ai-marketing"&gt;HubSpot’s 2025 AI Trends for Marketers report&lt;/a&gt;, and it’s clear that AI search is growing — rapidly. In 2026, Google reported that AI Mode has over one billion monthly users, and queries have doubled every quarter since launch.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Failure to place brands in &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/ai-overviews"&gt;AI Overviews&lt;/a&gt; (AIO) or within AI search tools like ChatGPT, Perplexity, or Claude is a failure to meet prospective buyers where they’re searching. That’s harmful to audience connection, conversion, and ultimately, revenue. Brands that show up in AI search are the ones that audiences consider. The ones that don’t simply disappear from the conversation, with no ranking position, no impression count, and no obvious way to tell.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;This article breaks down what brand visibility is, how to track brand visibility in AI search, the Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) that marketers need to pay attention to, and the best tools to support AI visibility tracking.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-is-ai-search-and-brand-visibility"&gt;What is AI search and brand visibility?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-track-brand-visibility-in-ai-search-right-now"&gt;How to Track Brand Visibility in AI Search Right Now.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-track-brand-visibility-in-ai-search-with-the-right-kpis-and-cadence"&gt;How to Track Brand Visibility in AI Search with the Right KPIs and Cadence&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-track-brand-visibility-in-ai-search-with-a-repeatable-system"&gt;How to Track Brand Visibility in AI Search with a Repeatable System&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-improve-ai-search-visibility-and-fix-inaccurate-answers"&gt;How to Improve AI Search Visibility and Fix Inaccurate Answers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#best-tools-to-track-brand-visibility-in-ai-search"&gt;Best Tools to Track Brand Visibility In AI Search&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-connect-ai-visibility-to-content-and-pipeline"&gt;How To Connect AI Visibility To Content And Pipeline&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-tracking-ai-search-visibility"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions About Tracking AI Search Visibility&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#tracking-ai-visibility-isnt-optional-anymore-search-changed"&gt;Tracking AI visibility isn’t optional anymore — search changed.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What is AI search and brand visibility?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AI search refers to search that takes place on AI platforms, like ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google Gemini, Microsoft Copilot, and Google’s AI Overviews. There are many more, and AI search platforms are growing. Unlike Google or other search engines, which return a list of links to click through, &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/ai-search-engines"&gt;AI search engines&lt;/a&gt; answer questions directly. Those answers are lifted or paraphrased from trusted sources.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Brand visibility in AI search relates to the impressions that brands get within AI platforms. A brand mentioned or cited in AI in an answer has visibility. Brand visibility in AI search includes mentions, citations, sentiment, and accuracy. The goal is for brands to increase their visibility. They want to be cited and mentioned often, accurately, and favorably.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;How to Track Brand Visibility in AI Search Right Now&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The most basic way to check AI brand visibility is manually: Open ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, and Copilot. Ask the same set of questions across each one. Then, record whether the brand appears, how it’s described, and whether competitors show up instead. This is an easy starting point. But, it breaks down quickly.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A single spot check only captures one moment in time. That result reflects one user’s search history and personalization, not any broader trend. When multiplied across several platforms and hundreds to thousands of prompt variations, manual tracking becomes a task that nobody has time to maintain.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;HubSpot &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/ran-ai-search-experiments"&gt;ran an experiment testing hundreds of queries&lt;/a&gt; across AI chatbots, search engines, and social platforms. The experiment found that AI tools were noticeably weaker at handling specific, niche information, like details about a particular local business, than they were at answering broad or general questions. This is why prompts need to be tracked consistently — and ideally automatically. No one can infer how a platform or brand performs across the board just because it performs well in one prompt, particularly if that prompt is broad and general.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;This is where dedicated tools come in.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Rather than replaying the same prompts by hand, tools built for AI brand tracking run them automatically, on a schedule, across multiple engines at once, then organize the results into a usable format, such as:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Which prompts triggered a mention.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Which sources got cited.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;How sentiment trended over time.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Different tools approach brand visibility measurement in different ways; some focus narrowly on mention frequency, others build out fuller scoring models across multiple dimensions.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/ai-search-grader/"&gt;HubSpot’s free AI Search Grader&lt;/a&gt; is one example. The grader gives marketers a baseline read on AI visibility, and what it provides for free is pretty amazing. Here’s what the start of the report looks like.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/Frank%20H/how-to-track-brand-visibility-in-ai-search-2-20260925-8838088.webp?width=450&amp;amp;height=506&amp;amp;name=how-to-track-brand-visibility-in-ai-search-2-20260925-8838088.webp" width="450" height="506" alt="Screenshot from HubSpot’s brand visibility tool, AI Search Grader, showing the key metrics and how they’re tracked across core AI platforms." style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 450px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;While tools like AI Search Grader are excellent, there are limitations.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AI Search Grader captures a baseline read; it doesn’t track improvements or declines in trends. Ideally, most marketing teams will move from a one-time snapshot to ongoing tracking, so that they can adapt marketing strategy based on data.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Tools like &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;Hub...

&lt;p&gt;I’ve been experimenting with Claude AI for marketing workflows over the past year, and it’s now my go-to assistant. In this field, AI use is close to universal: 98% of marketing teams use it in some way, according to &lt;a href="https://offers.hubspot.com/ai-marketing"&gt;HubSpot’s State of AI in Marketing report&lt;/a&gt;. For campaign marketers, that might look like turning a product announcement into a week of social posts, tightening ad copy to fit character limits, or pressure-testing campaign messaging before a stakeholder review.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=64493837-f4dd-43b0-abee-3ef154e06092&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Connect HubSpot to Claude For Personalized Insights [Free Connector]" height="58" width="645" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/64493837-f4dd-43b0-abee-3ef154e06092.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;But Claude only knows what you tell it. It can’t automatically see which contacts converted, which campaigns generated pipeline, or what customers keep asking your support team, so even sharp output can miss what’s actually happening in your business.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/claude"&gt;HubSpot connector for Claude&lt;/a&gt; brings your HubSpot CRM data into the conversation and lets Claude act on it, like drafting a marketing email or creating a follow-up task directly in your account. This guide covers how to set up the connector, the marketing workflows and prompts it supports, how to govern its use, and when a dashboard is the better choice.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-is-claude-ai-for-marketing"&gt;What is Claude AI for marketing?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#why-connect-claude-to-hubspot"&gt;Why Connect Claude to HubSpot?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-connect-claude-to-hubspot-using-the-hubspot-connector-for-claude"&gt;How to Connect Claude to HubSpot Using the HubSpot Connector for Claude&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#claude-ai-for-marketing-workflows-inside-hubspot"&gt;Claude AI for Marketing Workflows Inside HubSpot&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#claude-prompts-for-marketers-using-hubspot-context"&gt;Claude Prompts for Marketers Using HubSpot Context&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-govern-claude-ai-for-marketing-and-measure-impact"&gt;How to Govern Claude AI for Marketing and Measure Impact&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#when-to-use-dashboards-instead-of-claude-ai-for-marketing"&gt;When to Use Dashboards Instead of Claude AI for Marketing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-claude-ai-for-marketing"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions About Claude AI for Marketing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What is Claude AI for marketing?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Claude AI for marketing means using Claude, Anthropic’s AI assistant, to handle the writing, research, and analysis work that campaigns depend on. Claude helps marketers draft, analyze, and summarize work, such as writing and editing first drafts, turning meeting notes into briefs, and assembling campaign readouts from numbers in separate analytics tools. It can also pull current information from the web, which makes it handy for early-stage market research.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;As with all large language models (LLMs), the quality of Claude’s output depends heavily on the context it receives. &lt;a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/claude-prompting-best-practices"&gt;Anthropic’s prompting guidance&lt;/a&gt; compares Claude to a sharp new employee with no background on how your team operates, and it recommends telling Claude who the output is for and how it will be used.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Claude works well on its own for one-off drafting and research. It becomes far more powerful once it can read your real customer records, campaign results, and engagement history.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Why connect Claude to HubSpot?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Picture a marketer asking Claude why last quarter’s webinar series underperformed. Without a link to HubSpot, Claude can only work with what gets pasted into the chat: an exported spreadsheet, a few copied metrics, a paragraph describing the audience. Each fresh analysis means exporting and explaining that background again, and the answer stops wherever the export does.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Connected workflows move that context gathering out of the marketer’s hands. The HubSpot connector for Claude links HubSpot context to Claude, giving it read access to contacts, deals, campaigns, marketing emails, and other records, scoped to each person’s current HubSpot access rights. Logged calls, meetings, emails, tasks, and notes are readable too, unless the account has Sensitive Data turned on. The webinar question can now pull event records, follow-up activity, and campaign attribution data into a single answer.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The connection also runs in reverse. Claude can create and update HubSpot records, such as changing a deal stage or adding a task, from the chat window, though it can’t delete data.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;HubSpot Smart CRM unifies customer context and campaign records. It sits beneath Marketing Hub, Sales Hub, and HubSpot’s other core products as their shared database, showing where each contact stands at every point in the relationship. Claude then works from one consistent record rather than fragments stitched together from separate tools. Connected AI workflows improve &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/ai-personalization-growth"&gt;personalization&lt;/a&gt; and execution for that reason.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Getting there takes a one-time setup in Claude’s connector settings.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;How to Connect Claude to HubSpot Using the HubSpot Connector for Claude&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/test-2-20261030-4085970.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="Claude AI for marketing connectors list showing HubSpot integration with connect button"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/claude"&gt;HubSpot connector for Claude&lt;/a&gt; is free, but it requires a paid Claude plan (Pro, Max, Team, or Enterprise) and an active HubSpot user account on any plan, including free. Super Admins and users with App Marketplace Access permissions can connect immediately; everyone else needs Super Admin approval first.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Then, in Claude:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ol start="3"&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Log in to the HubSpot account you want to use.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Select the permissions to grant, then click &lt;strong&gt;Connect app&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ol&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;What the Connector Does&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/test-4-20261030-2782831.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="Claude AI for marketing welcome screen displaying daily pipeline pulse with HubSpot deals"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Toggling HubSpot on under &lt;strong&gt;+&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;gt; &lt;strong&gt;Connectors&lt;/strong&gt; in any chat lets Claude reference your HubSpot records in its answers. Set the connector’s &lt;em&gt;Write tools&lt;/em&gt; option to &lt;em&gt;Needs Approval&lt;/em&g...

&lt;p&gt;As you scroll through your TikTok or Instagram feed, you’ll no doubt come across at least a handful of influencers trying to sell you something by wearing the latest viral lip gloss, hopping into luxury cars, and taste-testing popular treats. But what if I told you that while these content creators may look like real people, they’re actually AI influencers?&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;If you’re a marketer or business owner who is already fully using AI in your digital marketing strategy, then you’re likely already familiar with the concept. You may even be curious about leveraging AI influencers in your influencer marketing strategy.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=b0f73a5e-16e4-41fd-9511-8564efc560a7&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Download Now: Free State of Marketing Report [Updated for 2026]" height="79" width="423" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/b0f73a5e-16e4-41fd-9511-8564efc560a7.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;But how will your target consumers feel about the use of AI influencers? Will they be receptive, or can AI influencers erode the trust you’ve built with your audience? Can AI influencers really save you money compared to working with human influencers? And are all virtual influencers AI? Keep reading for answers to these questions and more.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-are-ai-influencers-and-why-are-brands-considering-them"&gt;What are AI influencers, and why are brands considering them?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-do-consumers-think-about-ai-influencers-and-ai-models"&gt;What do consumers think about AI influencers and AI models?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#do-ai-influencers-build-or-erode-brand-trust"&gt;Do AI influencers build or erode brand trust?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#notable-virtual-influencers-brand-examples-to-learn-from"&gt;Notable Virtual Influencers + Brand Examples to Learn From&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#do-ai-influencers-save-brands-money"&gt;Do AI influencers save brands money?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-use-ai-assisted-content-workflows-without-losing-authenticity"&gt;How to Use AI-Assisted Content Workflows Without Losing Authenticity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#common-pitfalls-with-ai-influencers-and-how-to-avoid-backlash"&gt;Common Pitfalls With AI Influencers and How to Avoid Backlash&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#whats-next-for-ai-influencers"&gt;What’s Next for AI Influencers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-ai-influencers"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions About AI Influencers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What are AI influencers, and why are brands considering them?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AI influencers are virtual personas whose appearance, voice, behaviors, or content are created or assisted by generative AI. An example of an AI influencer is &lt;a href="https://www.instagram.com/fit_aitana/?hl%3Den"&gt;Aitana Lopez&lt;/a&gt;, who has over 400,000 followers on Instagram. She’s marketed as a virtual fitness and lifestyle influencer and has promoted brands such as Amazon, Victoria’s Secret, Olaplex, and Razer.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Her work as an influencer has reportedly earned her and The Clueless, the Barcelona-based tech company that created her, over &lt;a href="https://www.euronews.com/2024/12/27/meet-the-first-spanish-ai-model-earning-up-to-10000-per-month"&gt;$11,000 per month&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
